==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|lecherous}}, {{m|enm|licherous}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|*lecherous}} (attested in {{cog|fro|lecherousement||lecherously}}), from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|lecherie}}, {{m|fro|licherie||gluttony, sensuality, lewdness, lechery}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|lecher}}, {{m|fro|lechier}}, {{m|fro|lekier}}, {{m|fro|lescher||to lick, live in gluttony or sensuality}}, from Old {{etyl|frk|en}} {{m|frk|*lekkon|*lekkōn|to lick}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*likkōną||to lick}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*leyǵʰ-||to lick}}, equivalent to {{suffix|lecher|ous|lang=en}}. More at {{l|en|lick}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlɛtʃəɹəs/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Given to excessive sexual activity and [[debauchery]].

